    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        178,
        669,
        1521,
        743
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, since October 2022, over two hundred thousand asylum seekers have arrived in New York City from the Southern border without having any immediate plans for shelter; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.2555,
          "min": -1.2371
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0003,
          "min": -0.0003
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 36,
          "mean": -0.0005,
          "min": -0.0142
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 15253,
        "area_px": 95608,
        "density": 0.15954,
        "chars": 176,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 11.54
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        176,
        784,
        1521,
        927
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, the City continues to face an unprecedented humanitarian crisis that requires it to take extraordinary measures to meet the needs of the asylum seekers while continuing to serve the tens of thousands of people who currently use the Department of Homeless Services Shelter System; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.2585,
          "min": -1.3098
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 50,
          "mean": -0.0003,
          "min": -0.0099
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 24380,
        "area_px": 184756,
        "density": 0.13196,
        "chars": 292,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 11.98
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        176,
        977,
        1524,
        1095
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, the state of emergency based on the arrival of hundreds of thousands of individuals and families seeking asylum, first declared in Emergency Executive Order No. 224, dated October 7, 2022,\u00b9 and extended by subsequent orders, remains in effect; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.2321,
          "min": -1.2799
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 58,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.002
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 21262,
        "area_px": 153748,
        "density": 0.13829,
        "chars": 256,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 12.04
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        174,
        1142,
        1522,
        1340
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, additional measures continued in this order are set forth in Emergency Executive Order No. 230 of 2022, Emergency Executive Order No. 241 of 2022, Emergency Executive Order No. 302 of 2023, Emergency Executive Order No. 350 of 2023, Emergency Executive Order No. 386 of 2023, Emergency Executive Order No. 402 of 2023, and Emergency Executive Order No. 406 of 2023; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2147,
          "min": -1.1248
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 127,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0012
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 32513,
        "area_px": 255816,
        "density": 0.1271,
        "chars": 378,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 11.63
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        172,
        1392,
        1517,
        1591
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, this order consolidates the provisions of prior orders issued in response to the emergency first declared in Emergency Executive Order No. 224, limits the suspensions of laws and rules to those that are necessary to allow for the continued operation of facilities needed to address the asylum emergency, and ends the suspensions of laws and rules related to the New York City Landmarks Law and the Landmarks Preservation Commission;",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2117,
          "min": -1.1102
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 84,
          "mean": -0.0002,
          "min": -0.0108
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 35909,
        "area_px": 257108,
        "density": 0.13967,
        "chars": 441,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 12.28
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        172,
        1639,
        1517,
        1789
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "NOW, THEREFORE, pursuant to the powers vested in me by the laws of the State of New York and the City of New York, including but not limited to the New York Executive Law, the New York City Charter, the New York City Administrative Code, and the common law authority to protect the public in the event of an emergency:",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.225,
          "min": -1.1125
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
